{
  "name": "PDT pull request review",
  "description": "Each pull request PDT didn't open (an outsider's or a bot's) gets an external ticket. Dependabot's patch and minor updates merge once CI passes, with nothing in your Inbox unless it fails. Every other one is reviewed by the locked-down PR Reviewer from the diff GitHub gives (it never checks the code out or runs it), the review goes on the ticket, and your Inbox asks: Approve & merge (once CI passes), Request changes (posted on the pull request as a review; a push reviews it again) or Close (the ticket goes to Won't do). Nothing is posted on the pull request until you choose, and nothing is pushed to its branch. One merged or closed on GitHub finishes its ticket to match. Enabled where a project's repository is RossTools/PersonalDevTeam.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "opened",
      "kind": "github.pull_request.opened",
      "version": 1,
      "config": {
        "repos": [
          "RossTools/PersonalDevTeam"
        ]
      },
      "position": {
        "x": 0.0,
        "y": 0.0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "pushed",
      "kind": "github.pull_request.pushed",
      "version": 1,
      "config": {
